Day 55 of #DrGVishwanathanChallenge

Today, I solved another Binary Tree problem in Java 

Problem: 572. Subtree of Another Tree

Approach:
For this problem, I used recursion and tree traversal. I traversed through every node of the main tree and, at each node, checked whether the subtree starting from that node is identical to the given subRoot.

To compare two trees, I created a separate helper function, isSame(). This function checks whether both nodes have the same value and recursively verifies their left and right subtrees.

Key Concepts:
 Binary Trees
Recursion
 Tree Traversal
 Comparing Two Binary Trees

Time Complexity: O(m × n)
Space Complexity: O(h) due to the recursion stack.

A good problem for understanding how recursion can be used both to traverse a tree and compare two subtrees. Slowly getting more comfortable with Binary Tree problems! 💪🌳

